# 🦠 CovidLens: Exploratory Data Analysis on COVID-19 Data

An interactive dashboard that cleans raw COVID-19 data and turns it into trends, country rankings, vaccination progress and correlations. Built with **Python, Pandas, Streamlit and Plotly** using the Our World in Data (OWID) dataset.

Course project: Data Science Lab, Dept. of AI & DS, Francis Xavier Engineering College.

---

## Features

- **Data cleaning:** removes duplicates, aggregate rows (World, continents, income groups), negative values and missing entries
- **Derived metrics:** case fatality rate, cases per million, 7-day moving average
- **KPI cards:** total cases, total deaths, fatality rate, total vaccinations
- **Trend analysis:** daily (7-day average) and monthly new cases
- **Country analysis:** top 10 countries by total cases
- **Correlation heatmap:** cases, deaths, vaccinations and cases per million
- **Interactive filters:** country and date range, with all charts updating live
- **Data quality summary** and **CSV download** of the filtered data

## Project structure

```
covid19_project_report/
├── app.py                 # Streamlit dashboard (cleaning + analysis + charts)
├── owid-covid-data.csv    # Dataset (auto-downloaded on first run)
└── README.md
```

## Requirements

- Python 3.9 or newer
- Packages: `streamlit`, `pandas`, `plotly`

```bash
pip install streamlit pandas plotly
```

## How to run

```bash
cd covid19_project_report
streamlit run app.py
```

The app opens at `http://localhost:8501`.

## Dataset

Source: [Our World in Data, COVID-19 dataset](https://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/api/covid/)

On the first run, `app.py` downloads the compact CSV automatically from:

```
https://catalog.ourworldindata.org/garden/covid/latest/compact/compact.csv
```

and saves it as `owid-covid-data.csv` next to `app.py`. If the download fails (no internet or a blocked link), download the file manually from the page above and save it with that name in the project folder.

> Note: the old GitHub copy of the dataset (`owid/covid-19-data`) is no longer updated, so use the link above.

## How it works

1. **Load:** read the CSV and rename columns if needed
2. **Clean:** drop duplicates, remove aggregate rows, fix negatives, fill missing values
3. **Calculate:** fatality rate, cases per million, 7-day average
4. **Filter:** user selects countries and a date range
5. **Visualise:** KPIs, trend charts, top 10, heatmap
6. **Export:** download the filtered data as CSV

## Troubleshooting

| Problem                                  | Fix                                                                                                                     |
| ---------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `FileNotFoundError: owid-covid-data.csv` | Run `streamlit run app.py` from the project folder, or download the CSV manually                                        |
| `NameError: name 'df' is not defined`    | Make sure `df, raw_rows = load_data()` appears right after the `load_data()` function                                   |
| `KeyError` on a column name              | Print the columns with `pd.read_csv("owid-covid-data.csv", nrows=3).columns.tolist()` and adjust names in `load_data()` |

